---
title: Jalapeno Tacos
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3oFk6d7XNJ8
author: Adam Ragusea
cuisine: Mexican
---

Set a #cast-iron pan{} on medium low.

Drain one @can of black beans{15 oz}. Add to the pan with some @olive oil{1 tbsp} and let cook for ~{5 minutes} until warmed.

Crush about 1/3 of the beans to make a paste.

Dice some @jalapeno{1/4 cup} and add to the pan.

Add some @garlic powder{1 tsp}, @cumin{1 tsp}, onion powder{1 tsp}, curry powder{1 tsp}, and @salt{1 tsp}. Stir to combine, add a splash of water, and cook for another ~{5 minutes} until the beans are soft and a saucy texture is achieved.

Cube some @melting cheese{1/2 cup} and add to the pan. Stir until just melting, then remove from the heat.

Set another #cast-iron pan{} on medium low. Add a shallow layer of @olive oil{} and let it heat until shimmering.

One by one, fill a @tortilla{} with the bean mixture, roll up, and place seam side down in the pan. Cook until the bottom is browned, flip, and cook until done.